      "skills": "Developing and using models (revising the Lesson 1 model into a final model); analysing and interpreting data (comparing three machines); using mathematics (MA, VR, efficiency); constructing explanations (writing the Final Explanation with claim, evidence and reasoning); engaging in argument from evidence during the gallery walk.",
      "attitudes": "Curiosity and perseverance in resolving the puzzle of why the same energy feels easier to supply; honesty in reporting measured data including the energy that goes to heat; respect for others' ideas in peer critique; appreciation of simple machines in everyday Kenyan life (wells, wheelbarrows, lorries, crowbars).",
